  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts. It typechecks, but I had no shell or browser, so I haven't built it with `vite build` or looked at a rendered frame. The wave look, sun and moon positions, colours and brightness are untested.\n\n- **Island:** a flat-shaded low-poly island generated in code, with jittered grid vertices and one normal per face. It has sand, grass and rock colours by height, a central peak, about 26 pine trees and a handful of rocks.\n- **Water:** a large custom GLSL surface with animated sine waves and faceted normals. It has a fresnel mix with the sky, a sun/moon glint, a shallow tint and foam near the island, and it fades into the sky colour at distance.\n- **Day/night cycle:** one cycle takes 20 seconds, starting at hour 9. It moves the Preetham sky's sun, the sun and moon directional lights, and the hemisphere light's brightness and tint. It also changes the fog colour and the water shader's sky colour, light direction and brightness each frame. Night keeps a moon light and a minimum hemisphere intensity, so the scene should never go black.\n- **Camera:** an orbit camera at about [17, 11, 20], above the water and framing the island, rotating slowly. It uses `autoRotate: 0.12`.\n- **Ready flag:** `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set after `app.ready()` and two animation frames.\n\n",
